{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-language lease-key vectors (design 06 P4a).",
    "Read by BOTH shared/go/lease/key_test.go and",
    "shared/python/tests/test_lease_contract.py, so the Go and Python",
    "implementations are checked against the same expectations instead of",
    "against each other's source.",
    "Why a shared fixture: a lease key formatted differently in Go than in",
    "Python does not fail loudly. It produces a Redis miss, the gateway asks",
    "for a new lease, and a working copy already mounted elsewhere gets",
    "mounted a second time -- the exact corruption the lease prevents.",
    "Add a case here whenever either side's parsing changes."
  ],
